TraceUePositions
================

The class `NrSlTraceHelper` provides several helper methods to enable traces
and plots relevant to sidelink operation.  A basic trace and plotting script
to visualize UE mobility in a sidelink simulation is available with the
method `NrSlTraceHelper::TraceUePositions()` and the corresponding Bash
script `plot-ue-positions.sh` which can be found in the `examples/sl-examples`
directory.  The Bash script requires Gnuplot to be installed on the host.

The trace file can be generated by two statements such as the below. 

.. sourcecode:: cpp

  // UE positions tracing outputs NrSlUePositionTrace.txt
  NrSlTraceHelper nrSlTraceHelper;
  nrSlTraceHelper.TraceUePositions(relayUeNodes); 

Optional arguments to `TraceUePositions` include the option to configure the
polling interval and to change the trace filename. 

The trace file can be converted to a PDF file by using the provided Bash script,
such as follows.

.. sourcecode:: shell

  $ contrib/nr/examples/sl-examples/plot-ue-positions.sh NrSlUePositionTrace.txt

The above will yield a `ue-positions.pdf` file such as the example below (illustrating motion of
two relay nodes for 15 seconds of simulation time, in this case).

